Author: Sean Pedersen <seanpedersen96@protonmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 15:29:06 2026 +0100

    Reduce narrow fast-mode serving RAM without changing codes
    
    Regenerate scaled basis coefficients from the serving model while retaining centroid projection panels and ordered FP32 arithmetic. Preserve serialized indexes, threshold-5 routing, high-bit precision and append ownership.
    
    Add projection and persistence tests plus full-data OpenAI allocation, dual disk/RAM budget and timing evidence. At 1695 code bits, RAM falls 14.2% at identical recall; spending the saving on 2048 bits reaches recall 0.9192 within RaBitQ's 2-bit disk and RAM budgets. Document the measured throughput and latency tradeoffs.

